caraz"}}}}},{"id":160065,"type":"athlete","uid":"s:850~l:851~a:2946","guid":"6493155f-cacc-7aa5-ba78-d952efa4c652","description":"Taylor Fritz","sportId":851,"athleteId":2946,"athlete":{"id":2946,"description":"Taylor Fritz","links":{"mobile":{"athletes":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/tennis/player/_/id/2946/taylor-fritz"}},"web":{"athletes":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/tennis/player/_/id/2946/taylor-fritz"}}}}},{"id":574345,"type":"athlete","uid":"s:850~l:851~a:9250","guid":"2358bec1-f6f0-3540-a37e-13bc322d2c08","description":"Ben Shelton","sportId":851,"athleteId":9250,"athlete":{"id":9250,"description":"Ben Shelton","links":{"mobile":{"athletes":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/tennis/player/_/id/9250/ben-shelton"}},"web":{"athletes":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/tennis/player/_/id/9250/ben-shelton"}}}}},{"id":380957,"type":"athlete","uid":"s:850~l:851~a:2964","guid":"8965d2eb-1419-a6e6-5d3f-573b8b0bc565","description":"Tommy Paul","sportId":851,"athleteId":2964,"athlete":{"id":2964,"description":"Tommy Paul","links":{"mobile":{"athletes":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/tennis/player/_/id/2964/tommy-paul"}},"web":{"athletes":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/tennis/player/_/id/2964/tommy-paul"}}}}}],"keywords":["news","ATP","Carlos Alcaraz","Taylor Fritz","Ben Shelton","Tommy Paul"],"story":"<p>PARIS -- <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/sports/tennis/players/profile?playerId=3782\">Carlos Alcaraz</a> saved two match points against <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/sports/tennis/players/profile?playerId=2946\">Taylor Fritz</a> to reach the Paris Masters semifinals on Friday and the field for the ATP Finals was settled.</p>\n<p>Alcaraz was match point down in the second set at 5-3 and 5-4, saving the second with a forehand pass. He finally won 6-7 (10), 7-5, 6-3.</p>\n<p>\"I tried not to let myself down in the difficult moments in the second set,\" Alcaraz said. \"I tried to stay strong mentally and save those break points and match points.</p>\n<p><alsosee></p>\n<p>\"I would say 3-5 serving, that game we played incredible tennis. I used the people and the energy and gave them what they really wanted to watch and I am really happy to play for one and a half hours more to entertain them. The feeling I have today is unmatched.\"</p>\n<p>Alcaraz will feature in the Paris semifinals for the first time. The seven-time Grand Slam champion has been hampered by <a href=\"https://apnews.com/article/us-open-carlos-alcaraz-breaks-73f241e13a891601d987081fc39a620a\">injury and fatigue</a> this year. But he won the Vienna title last week and looks fresher than many of his rivals at this stage of the season.</p>\n<p><a href=\"http://www.espn.com/sports/tennis/players/profile?playerId=9250\">Ben Shelton</a> also reached his first Paris semifinal after winning an all-American matchup against <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/sports/tennis/players/profile?playerId=2964\">Tommy Paul</a> 6-4, 4-6, 6-3.</p>\n<p>Shelton, with 19 aces, converted two of four break points. It was his third win in five meetings between them.</p>\n<p>Shelton ended Paul's hopes of qualifying for the ATP Finals in Turin this month. As a result, another American player, <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/sports/tennis/players/profile?playerId=2708\">Frances Tiafoe</a>, clinched a spot and will debut at the tournament. Fritz's loss qualified <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/sports/tennis/players/profile?playerId=12657\">Rafael Jodar</a> in the eighth and last spot.</p>\n<p>The other qualifiers for the Finals are top-ranked <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/sports/tennis/players/profile?playerId=2375\">Alexander Zverev</a>, Alcaraz, Shelton, <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/sports/tennis/players/profile?playerId=2383\">Daniil Medvedev</a>, <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/sports/tennis/players/profile?playerId=7602\">Flavio Cobolli</a> and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/sports/tennis/players/profile?playerId=10052\">Arthur Fils</a>.</p>\n<p>Shelton will next play local <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/sports/tennis/players/profile?playerId=8814\">Luca Van Assche</a>, who took almost three hours to defeat qualifier <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/sports/tennis/players/profile?playerId=3716\">Rinky Hijikata</a> 6-4, 6-7 (4), 7-5. Alcaraz will take on <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/sports/tennis/players/profile?playerId=2989\">Casper Ruud</a> or <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/sports/tennis/players/profile?playerId=4115\">Nuno Borges</a>.</p>\n\n","allowAMP":true,"allowAds":true,"allowComments":true,"allowCommerce":true,"allowContentReactions":true,"allowSearch":true,"isLiveBlog":false,"links":{"api":{"self":{"href":"https://content.core.api.espn.com/v1/sports/news/50402471"}},"app":{"sportscenter":{"href":"sportscenter://x-callback-url/showStory?uid=50402471"}},"mobile":{"href":"http://m.espn.go.com/general/tennis/story?storyId=50402471"},"web":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/tennis/story/_/id/50402471/alacaraz-shelton-advance-semifinals-paris-masters"}},"premium":false},{"id":50402469,"nowId":"1-50402469","contentKey":"50402469-1-5-1","dataSourceIdentifier":"5f98f434cfb0e","publishedkey":"50402469","type":"HeadlineNews","feedDisplayType":"Default","headline":"NCAA secures win in struggle for five-year eligibility rule","description":"Federal appeals court judges handed the NCAA a significant victory in its struggle to implement a new five-year eligibility ruling Friday, though the win does nothing to tamp down dozens of similar lawsuits playing out in state courts across the country.","title":"NCAA secures win in struggle for five-year eligibility rule","linkText":"Appeals court hands NCAA victory in struggle for five-year eligibility rule","categorized":"2026-11-06T22:51:37Z","originallyPosted":"2026-11-06T22:50:46Z","lastModified":"2026-11-06T22:51:37Z","published":"2026-11-06T22:51:37Z","root":"ncaa","section":"College Football","source":"Associated Press","images":[{"dataSourceIdentifier":"1e3fc32bc3ecf","id":50402414,"type":"header","name":"NCAA Flag [600x600]","credit":"Icon Sportswire","height":600,"width":600,"url":"https://a.espncdn.com/photo/2026/1106/r1742187_600x600_1-1.jpg"}],"related":[{"id":50338950,"dataSourceIdentifier":"1b2b7bc2c57ed","publishedkey":"50338950","type":"HeadlineNews","headline":"Castellanos gets start, lifts Texas Tech to win over Arizona","title":"Castellanos gets start, lifts Texas Tech to win over Arizona","linkText":"Castellanos gives Texas Tech 'juice' in bounce-back win over Arizona","images":[{"dataSourceIdentifier":"9b417d5a9ba01","id":50338169,"type":"header","name":"Thomas Castellanos #4 of the Texas Tech Red Raiders runs with the ball photodesk [600x400]","credit":"John E. Moore III/Getty Images","height":400,"width":600,"url":"https://a.espncdn.com/photo/2026/1031/r1739046_600x400_3-2.jpg"}],"byline":"Dave Wilson","isLiveBlog":false,"links":{"api":{"self":{"href":"https://content.core.api.espn.com/v1/sports/news/50338950"}},"app":{"sportscenter":{"href":"sportscenter://x-callback-url/showStory?uid=50338950"}},"mobile":{"href":"http://m.espn.go.com/ncf/story?storyId=50338950"},"web":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50338950/castellanos-starts-guides-texas-tech-win-arizona"}},"premium":false},{"id":50401639,"dataSourceIdentifier":"d479b8dc6f370","publishedkey":"50401639","type":"HeadlineNews","headline":"Sources: SEC considering luxury tax for excessive spending on players","title":"Sources - SEC mulls luxury tax for overspending on players","linkText":"Sources: SEC considering luxury tax for excessive spending on players","images":[{"dataSourceIdentifier":"86741cab1ded5","id":49716960,"type":"header","name":"SEC [1296x729]","credit":"Imagn Images","height":729,"width":1296,"url":"https://a.espncdn.com/photo/2026/0825/r1706540_1296x729_16-9.jpg"}],"byline":"Mark Schlabach and Pete Thamel","isLiveBlog":false,"links":{"api":{"self":{"href":"https://content.core.api.espn.com/v1/sports/news/50401639"}},"app":{"sportscenter":{"href":"sportscenter://x-callback-url/showStory?uid=50401639"}},"mobile":{"href":"http://m.espn.go.com/ncf/story?storyId=50401639"},"web":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50401639/sources-sec-mulls-luxury-tax-overspending-players"}},"premium":false},{"id":50372965,"dataSourceIdentifier":"40fd1d7d39cd7","publishedkey":"50372965","type":"Story","headline":"Ranking college football's top 40 freshmen in 2026","title":"Ranking college football's top 40 freshmen in 2026","linkText":"Updated rankings of the top 40 freshmen in college football","images":[{"dataSourceIdentifier":"3442d97ca4339","id":50379598,"type":"header","name":"Deuce Geralds [608x342]","caption":"LSU's Deuce Geralds has established himself as the most impactful freshman on the defensive line in the country.","credit":"Stew Milne/Getty Images","height":342,"width":608,"url":"https://a.espncdn.com/photo/2026/1104/r1741029_608x342_16-9.jpg"}],"byline":"Billy Tucker","isLiveBlog":false,"links":{"api":{"self":{"href":"https://content.core.api.espn.com/v1/sports/news/50372965"}},"app":{"sportscenter":{"href":"sportscenter://x-callback-url/showStory?uid=50372965"}},"mobile":{"href":"http://m.espn.go.com/ncf/story?storyId=50372965"},"web":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50372965/ranking-college-football-top-40-freshmen-2026"}},"premium":false}],"categories":[{"id":9571,"type":"league","uid":"s:20~l:23","guid":"0f8e3d42-fa27-3f60-9e8d-276e4892f50e","description":"NCAA Football","sportId":23,"leagueId":23,"league":{"id":23,"description":"NCAA Football","abbreviation":"NCAAF","links":{"mobile":{"leagues":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/"}},"web":{"leagues":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/"}}}}},{"id":14486,"type":"league","guid":"d765930d-4c8c-47ed-8b85-8f1955d4a602","description":"NCAA - Other sports","sportId":0,"leagueId":3170,"league":{"id":3170,"description":"NCAA - Other sports"}},{"id":9576,"type":"league","uid":"s:40~l:41","guid":"11965179-4504-3b99-983e-83ea0e36d5f3","description":"NCAA Men's Basketball","sportId":41,"leagueId":41,"league":{"id":41,"description":"NCAA Men's Basketball","abbreviation":"NCAAM","links":{"mobile":{"leagues":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/mens-college-basketball/"}},"web":{"leagues":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/mens-college-basketball/"}}}}},{"id":9578,"type":"league","uid":"s:40~l:54","guid":"45cd175c-f9f2-338b-83b9-6d7d64001733","description":"NCAA Women's Basketball","sportId":54,"leagueId":54,"league":{"id":54,"description":"NCAA Women's Basketball","abbreviation":"NCAAW","links":{"mobile":{"leagues":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/womens-college-basketball/"}},"web":{"leagues":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/womens-college-basketball/"}}}}},{"id":116550,"type":"topic","guid":"fe879255-6324-4784-385f-a1a18c22b5cc","description":"espnw","sportId":0,"topicId":5}],"keywords":["NCAA Football","NCAA - Other sports","NCAA Men's Basketball","NCAA Women's Basketball","espnw"],"story":"<p>DENVER -- Federal appeals court judges handed the NCAA a significant victory in its struggle to implement a new five-year eligibility ruling Friday, though the win does nothing to tamp down dozens of similar lawsuits playing out in state courts across the country.</p>\n<p>Ruling in the case Wisne vs. NCAA, the 10th Circuit Court of Appeals in Denver reversed a lower-court decision that had granted players across the country who graduated high school in 2022 a fifth year of eligibility.</p>\n<p>The lower-court ruling in July went against the NCAA's new rule that granted five years of eligibility, but only starting with athletes from the next year's class. It essentially made all those Class of '22 players eligible, leading to nationwide chaos, with teams looking to sign players who had been relegated to the sideline.</p>\n<p>But in August, when this same appeals court first put the ruling on hold, many of those players still found their way onto rosters thanks to favorable rulings in state courts.</p>\n<p><alsosee></p>\n<p>The decision Friday doesn't resolve some 200 state cases that involve as many as 850 athletes. The NCAA applauded it nonetheless, with chief legal officer Scott Bearby calling it \"consistent with the approach taken by every federal court of appeals\" in cases like these.</p>\n<p>\"The decision also acknowledges the NCAA's concern that retroactively changing eligibility rules can destabilize rosters and disrupt the settled expectations of student-athletes regarding roster spots and playing time,\" Bearby wrote in a memo to NCAA members.</p>\n<p>Much of that damage has already been done, as football's regular season heads into its final month with some players -- for instance, Texas Tech quarterback Thomas Castellanos -- toggling on and off rosters depending on the latest court ruling. Basketball season started this week under similar uncertainty.</p>\n<p>The decision hinged over what judges said was the plaintiffs' inability to define the market for players -- a key point in determining how those players are being harmed by being declared ineligible.</p>\n<p>In the decision penned by Judge Carolyn McHugh, the three-judge panel knocked down the plaintiff argument that all Division I players, regardless of sport, formed a single market.</p>\n<p>\"Obviously, a football player looking for a Division I roster spot would not view the 101 schools without a football program as reasonably good substitutes,\" McHugh wrote.</p>\n\n","allowAMP":true,"allowAds":true,"allowComments":true,"allowCommerce":true,"allowContentReactions":true,"allowSearch":true,"isLiveBlog":false,"links":{"api":{"self":{"href":"https://content.core.api.espn.com/v1/sports/news/50402469"}},"app":{"sportscenter":{"href":"sportscenter://x-callback-url/showStory?uid=50402469"}},"mobile":{"href":"http://m.espn.go.com/extra/ncaa/story?storyId=50402469"},"web":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/college-sports/story/_/id/50402469/ncaa-secures-win-struggle-five-year-eligibility-rule"}},"premium":false},{"id":50402463,"nowId":"1-50402463","contentKey":"50402463-1-5-1","dataSourceIdentifier":"3d417c3fb4b77","publishedkey":"50402463","type":"HeadlineNews","feedDisplayType":"Default","headline":"Nick Bosa back, Christian McCaffrey good to go for Niners","description":"The 49ers will have a healthy Nick Bosa for the first time since Week 2, and running back Christian McCaffrey is good to go this week against the Raiders.","title":"Nick Bosa back, Christian McCaffrey good to go for Niners","linkText":"Bosa (calf) returns, McCaffrey (hamstring) good to go for Niners","categorized":"2026-11-06T23:03:00Z","originallyPosted":"2026-11-06T22:49:59Z","lastModified":"2026-11-06T23:03:00Z","published":"2026-11-06T23:03:00Z","root":"nfl","section":"NFL","images":[{"dataSourceIdentifier":"bff77f6571d05","id":49238800,"type":"header","name":"Nick Bosa [1296x729]","alt":"Nick Bosa","credit":"Robin Alam/Icon Sportswire","height":729,"width":1296,"url":"https://a.espncdn.com/photo/2026/0701/r1682817_1296x729_16-9.jpg"},{"type":"Media","name":"Where the 49ers stand at WR ahead of Week 9 and the trade deadline","caption":"Nick Wagoner discusses the wide receivers the 49ers are getting back from injury as the trade deadline approaches.","height":324,"width":576,"url":"https://espnmedia-cdn.akamaized.net/espn/media/common/2026/1105/dm_261105_Niners_WRs_IA/dm_261105_Niners_WRs_IA.jpg"}],"video":[{"id":50394711,"dataSourceIdentifier":"acfd0d531f670","cerebroId":"6aed2f03f141af21719ce788","pccId":"31e28c15-705e-4238-89c8-7ff0f381acc7","source":"espn","headline":"Where the 49ers stand at WR ahead of Week 9 and the trade deadline","shortHeadline":"Where the 49ers stand at WR ahead of Week 9 and the trade deadline","caption":"Nick Wagoner discusses the wide receivers the 49ers are getting back from injury as the trade deadline approaches.","title":"Where the 49ers stand at WR ahead of Week 9 and the trade deadline","description":"Nick Wagoner discusses the wide receivers the 49ers are getting back from injury as the trade dea