:[{"dataSourceIdentifier":"825c1a2d72b88","id":50358817,"type":"header","name":"Josh Allen [1296x729]","caption":"Josh Allen and the Buffalo Bills head to Minnesota as slight favorites in Monday night's matchup with the Vikings.","alt":"Josh Allen runs the ball for the Buffalo Bills.","credit":"Timothy T Ludwig/Getty Images","height":729,"width":1296,"url":"https://a.espncdn.com/photo/2026/1102/r1740078_1296x729_16-9.jpg"}],"byline":"ESPN","isLiveBlog":false,"links":{"api":{"self":{"href":"https://content.core.api.espn.com/v1/sports/news/50358691"}},"app":{"sportscenter":{"href":"sportscenter://x-callback-url/showStory?uid=50358691"}},"mobile":{"href":"http://m.espn.go.com/wireless/story?storyId=50358691"},"web":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/espn/betting/story/_/id/50358691/2026-nfl-week-9-schedule-odds-point-spreads-totals"}},"premium":false}],"categories":[{"id":9572,"type":"league","uid":"s:20~l:28","guid":"ad4c3bd2-ddb6-3f8c-8abf-744855a08fa4","description":"NFL","sportId":28,"leagueId":28,"league":{"id":28,"description":"NFL","abbreviation":"NFL","links":{"mobile":{"leagues":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/"}},"web":{"leagues":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/"}}}}},{"id":1637,"type":"team","uid":"s:20~l:28~t:25","guid":"985a261f-296c-c95c-32a5-addc4df75001","description":"San Francisco 49ers","sportId":28,"teamId":25,"team":{"id":25,"description":"San Francisco 49ers","abbreviation":"SF","shortDisplayName":"49ers","links":{"mobile":{"teams":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/team/_/name/sf/san-francisco-49ers"}},"web":{"teams":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/team/_/name/sf/san-francisco-49ers"}}}}},{"id":409224,"type":"topic","guid":"52313677-19f8-b106-ec91-d8d17e6087fe","description":"news","sportId":0,"topicId":781},{"id":379795,"type":"athlete","uid":"s:20~l:28~a:4040605","guid":"6a5ec871-ae65-1fde-4664-f513284ad1ba","description":"Nick Bosa","sportId":28,"athleteId":4040605,"athlete":{"id":4040605,"description":"Nick Bosa","links":{"mobile":{"athletes":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4040605/nick-bosa"}},"web":{"athletes":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4040605/nick-bosa"}}}}},{"id":166874,"type":"athlete","uid":"s:20~l:28~a:3117251","guid":"db08ac19-dbd9-a776-5885-de1fe6830bc2","description":"Christian McCaffrey","sportId":28,"athleteId":3117251,"athlete":{"id":3117251,"description":"Christian McCaffrey","links":{"mobile":{"athletes":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/3117251/christian-mccaffrey"}},"web":{"athletes":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/3117251/christian-mccaffrey"}}}}},{"id":126377,"type":"athlete","uid":"s:20~l:28~a:16737","guid":"5073fc58-91c1-4e3d-826d-af754f9f40c7","description":"Mike Evans","sportId":28,"athleteId":16737,"athlete":{"id":16737,"description":"Mike Evans","links":{"mobile":{"athletes":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/16737/mike-evans"}},"web":{"athletes":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/16737/mike-evans"}}}}},{"id":696302,"type":"contributor","guid":"138f8e60-058f-3c5a-9eb4-7dcd2f50d36d","description":"Nick Wagoner","slug":"nick-wagoner","contributor":{"id":2313,"description":"Nick Wagoner"}}],"keywords":["NFL","San Francisco 49ers","news","Nick Bosa","Christian McCaffrey","Mike Evans","Nick Wagoner"],"story":"<p>SANTA CLARA, Calif. -- The <a data-clubhouse-guid=\"985a261f-296c-c95c-32a5-addc4df75001\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/team/_/name/sf/san-francisco-49ers\">San Francisco 49ers</a> will welcome defensive end <a data-player-guid=\"6a5ec871-ae65-1fde-4664-f513284ad1ba\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4040605/nick-bosa\">Nick Bosa</a> (calf) and running back <a data-player-guid=\"db08ac19-dbd9-a776-5885-de1fe6830bc2\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/3117251/christian-mccaffrey\">Christian McCaffrey</a> (hamstring) back from injury Sunday while receiver <a data-player-guid=\"5073fc58-91c1-4e3d-826d-af754f9f40c7\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/16737/mike-evans\">Mike Evans</a> will miss his second consecutive game because of Achilles tendinitis.</p>\n<p>Bosa, who has been out since before a Week 3 game against <a data-clubhouse-guid=\"8fc7b962-95e1-3cb8-6a7d-b499de9ad546\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/team/_/name/ari/arizona-cardinals\">Arizona Cardinals</a>, returned to practice this week and participated in some capacity for all three sessions this week. He has no injury designation for Sunday against the <a data-clubhouse-guid=\"b18540eb-6f2b-534c-e7f9-9bd930518da9\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/team/_/name/lv/las-vegas-raiders\">Las Vegas Raiders</a> and is good to go.</p>\n<p>\"I feel great,\" Bosa said. \"Bye week was a good extra week for me and I'm ready to go.\"</p>\n<p>Likewise, McCaffrey also does not have an injury designation after suffering a minor hamstring strain in Week 7 against the <a data-clubhouse-guid=\"49fd392a-86fe-4df3-1b77-9bbfa18b2ad5\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/team/_/name/atl/atlanta-falcons\">Atlanta Falcons</a>. McCaffrey did not practice Wednesday but participated on Thursday and Friday on his way to being cleared.</p>\n<p><alsosee></p>\n<p>Much like Bosa, McCaffrey said the Week 8 bye helped his recovery so he would not miss any time.</p>\n<p>\"It wasn't too bad,\" McCaffrey said. \"I think having the bye week was awesome, but I feel great.\"</p>\n<p>Evans, meanwhile, continues to deal with Achilles tendinitis that flared up in a Week 6 win against the <a data-clubhouse-guid=\"fbeaf73e-6d6c-cca4-0809-713d9d741f90\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/team/_/name/wsh/washington-commanders\">Washington Commanders</a>. He did not play against the Falcons and then had the bye week to continue recovering.</p>\n<p>Although Evans has made \"a lot of progress,\" according to coach Kyle Shanahan, the Niners don't want to risk pushing him too hard too soon so his injury doesn't get worse.</p>\n<p>\"I think you learn from the history,\" general manager John Lynch told KNBR radio in San Francisco on Thursday. \"Christian had this situation and every player is different, every situation is different but you don't want it to become something that really lingers. So, we're trying to knock it out such that when he comes back, we give him the best chance to stay back.\"</p>\n<p>In addition to Evans, the Niners ruled out fellow wideouts <a data-player-guid=\"7f300cb7-f0a1-a43a-d0b0-f8a57bf04eb3\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/3126486/deebo-samuel-sr\">Deebo Samuel Sr</a>. (hamstring) and <a data-player-guid=\"0c22d637-c0d7-6bac-7333-dc3a992bdc0d\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/3895856/christian-kirk\">Christian Kirk</a> (knee) for Sunday. Kirk injured his meniscus in practice Wednesday. It's unclear whether Kirk will need surgery, Shanahan said.</p>\n<p>In better receiver news, Shanahan said it's likely the team will activate <a data-player-guid=\"31f80c0b-02ca-cf2f-2fc3-669604f71430\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/3043116/demarcus-robinson\">Demarcus Robinson</a> (ankle) from injured reserve to play against the Raiders. That would leave a group of Robinson, <a data-player-guid=\"280e4563-f82e-37a3-a9ea-fd1a0232346f\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4431466/jordan-watkins\">Jordan Watkins</a>, <a data-player-guid=\"788f8622-3564-9d11-752d-1265e7c75c91\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4575665/jacob-cowing\">Jacob Cowing</a>, <a data-player-guid=\"e6108d57-ec3b-2e99-7260-781af58bb13c\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/16731/brandin-cooks\">Brandin Cooks</a> and, likely, <a data-player-guid=\"da675704-aeba-bd90-bbc6-03f72e44f6bd\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/3047876/khadarel-hodge\">KhaDarel Hodge</a> being elevated from the practice squad, as the team's receivers for Sunday.</p>\n<p>The 49ers listed Robinson, cornerback <a data-player-guid=\"1b718dbd-81cd-4fc2-ad85-60091ad65be4\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4240542/nate-hobbs\">Nate Hobbs</a> (adductor), safety <a data-player-guid=\"4c4be385-852d-a7b0-5953-9363be58fd36\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/3057524/siran-neal\">Siran Neal</a> (knee, foot) and cornerback <a data-player-guid=\"ae80113a-905c-37f7-9a7d-040f343a68c6\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4565200/upton-stout\">Upton Stout</a> (shoulder) as questionable for Sunday. Shanahan said it remains up in the air on whether they'll activate Hobbs from injured reserve this week.</p>\n\n\n\n\n","allowAMP":true,"allowAds":true,"allowComments":true,"allowCommerce":true,"allowContentReactions":false,"allowSearch":true,"byline":"Nick Wagoner","isLiveBlog":false,"links":{"api":{"self":{"href":"https://content.core.api.espn.com/v1/sports/news/50402463"}},"app":{"sportscenter":{"href":"sportscenter://x-callback-url/showStory?uid=50402463"}},"mobile":{"href":"http://m.espn.go.com/nfl/story?storyId=50402463"},"web":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50402463/nick-bosa-back-christian-mccaffrey-good-go-niners"}},"premium":false},{"id":50402359,"nowId":"1-50402359","contentKey":"50402359-1-5-1","dataSourceIdentifier":"7f4263d2ba42f","publishedkey":"50402359","type":"HeadlineNews","feedDisplayType":"Default","headline":"Caribbean Football Union endorses Infantino ahead of FIFA presidential election","description":"The Caribbean Football Union has endorsed Gianni Infantino following regional consultations, boosting his bid ahead of the FIFA presidential March election.","title":"Caribbean Football Union endorses Infantino for another term as FIFA president","linkText":"Infantino secures Caribbean soccer support for FIFA reelection bid","categorized":"2026-11-06T22:59:45Z","originallyPosted":"2026-11-06T22:36:54Z","lastModified":"2026-11-06T22:59:45Z","published":"2026-11-06T22:59:45Z","root":"soccer","section":"Soccer","source":"AP","images":[{"dataSourceIdentifier":"eb8533836870c","id":50402429,"type":"header","name":"Infantino [1296x729]","credit":"Photo by Fabio Deinert - FIFA/FIFA via Getty Images","height":729,"width":1296,"url":"https://a.espncdn.com/photo/2026/1106/r1742190_1296x729_16-9.jpg"}],"related":[{"id":50399850,"dataSourceIdentifier":"dfa321f79a04c","publishedkey":"50399850","type":"HeadlineNews","headline":"FIFA's chief legal officer steps down in second high-profile exit","title":"FIFA's chief legal officer steps down in second high-profile exit","linkText":"FIFA's chief legal officer steps down in second high-profile exit","images":[{"dataSourceIdentifier":"62c6e7c48ea85","id":48471799,"type":"header","name":"fifa [1296x729]","caption":"FIFA has written to Anthony Albanese urging the federal government to help support the construction of a permanent home of football as Australia risks losing pace with the world's leading nations.","credit":"Mustafa Yalcin/Anadolu via Getty Images","height":729,"width":1296,"url":"https://a.espncdn.com/photo/2026/0413/r1642668_1296x729_16-9.jpg"}],"byline":"ESPN News Services","isLiveBlog":false,"links":{"api":{"self":{"href":"https://content.core.api.espn.com/v1/sports/news/50399850"}},"app":{"sportscenter":{"href":"sportscenter://x-callback-url/showStory?uid=50399850"}},"mobile":{"href":"http://m.espn.go.com/soccer/story?storyId=50399850"},"web":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/soccer/story/_/id/50399850/fifa-chief-legal-compliance-officer-steps-down"}},"premium":false},{"id":50387286,"dataSourceIdentifier":"3a9a87a35d547","publishedkey":"50387286","type":"HeadlineNews","headline":"FIFA Council's Tashima to challenge Infantino in March elections - reports","title":"FIFA Council's Tashima to run against Infantino - reports","linkText":"Reports: FIFA Council's Tashima to challenge Infantino in March elections","source":"AP","images":[{"dataSourceIdentifier":"3b831b6b90cb7","id":28917501,"type":"header","name":"Kozo Tashima [1296x729]","alt":"Kozo Tashima","credit":"AP Photo/Shizuo Kambayashi","height":729,"width":1296,"url":"https://a.espncdn.com/photo/2020/0317/r680435_1296x729_16-9.jpg"}],"byline":"Associated Press","isLiveBlog":false,"links":{"api":{"self":{"href":"https://content.core.api.espn.com/v1/sports/news/50387286"}},"app":{"sportscenter":{"href":"sportscenter://x-callback-url/showStory?uid=50387286"}},"mobile":{"href":"http://m.espn.go.com/soccer/story?storyId=50387286"},"web":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/soccer/story/_/id/50387286/fifa-council-japan-tashima-challenge-infantino-reports"}},"premium":false},{"id":50358121,"dataSourceIdentifier":"a9ce51511f945","publishedkey":"50358121","type":"HeadlineNews","headline":"Source: FIFA to open World Cup private equity plan files following UEFA demands","title":"Source: FIFA to share World Cup private equity files after UEFA pressure","linkText":"Source: FIFA to share World Cup private equity files after UEFA pressure","images":[{"dataSourceIdentifier":"f63dbc2a2fc1a","id":49869930,"type":"header","name":"Infantino 2026 [1296x729]","caption":"FIFA will share confidential files on its scrapped World Cup sell-off plan with ruling Council members.","alt":"The President of FIFA, Gianni Infantino watches the Poland vs Argentina FIFA U-20 Women's World Cup first-round match on September 5, 2026 in Katowice, Poland. (","credit":"Omar Marques/Getty Images","height":729,"width":1296,"url":"https://a.espncdn.com/photo/2026/0908/r1713266_1296x729_16-9.jpg"}],"byline":"ESPN News Services","isLiveBlog":false,"links":{"api":{"self":{"href":"https://content.core.api.espn.com/v1/sports/news/50358121"}},"app":{"sportscenter":{"href":"sportscenter://x-callback-url/showStory?uid=50358121"}},"mobile":{"href":"http://m.espn.go.com/soccer/story?storyId=50358121"},"web":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/soccer/story/_/id/50358121/fifa-open-world-cup-private-equity-files-uefa-demands"}},"premium":false}],"categories":[{"id":81497,"type":"league","uid":"s:600","guid":"119cfa41-71d4-39bf-a790-6273a52b0259","description":"Soccer","sportId":600,"leagueId":600,"league":{"id":600,"description":"Soccer","links":{"mobile":{"leagues":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/soccer/"}},"web":{"leagues":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/soccer/"}}}}},{"id":33303,"type":"league","uid":"s:600~l:606","guid":"34f478c4-cf9a-35da-abd5-33db021e09d2","description":"FIFA World Cup","sportId":600,"leagueId":4,"league":{"id":606,"description":"FIFA World Cup","abbreviation":"FIFA World Cup","links":{"mobile":{"leagues":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/soccer/worldcup/"}},"web":{"leagues":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/soccer/worldcup/"}}}}}],"keywords":["Soccer","FIFA World Cup"],"story":"<p>The Caribbean Football Union announced on Friday it will endorse Gianni Infantino for another term as FIFA president in the election in March.</p>\n<p>Infantino recently made two trips to the Caribbean, including this week, to secure the bloc's support despite lingering controversy over his aborted World Cup investment plan.</p>\n<p>\"The CFU emphasizes that it determined its collective position through consultation with its member associations,\" the organization said in a statement. \"In this same spirit the CFU continues to call for increased transparency, good governance, and meaningful reform within the football family.\"<br>\n<br>\n<alsosee></p>\n<p>The CFU has 31 member nations, 25 of which hold voting rights.</p>\n<p>This marks the second major voting bloc to publicly declare its backing for Infantino. Last month, the Asian Football Confederation, which represents 47 member associations, endorsed him for another term.</p>\n<p>The filing deadline for candidates is Nov. 18. The first challenger emerged when FIFA council member Kohzo Tashima - a colleague of Infantino for nearly 11 years - announced on Thursday he intends to run for president.</p>\n<p>Infantino's reelection prospects have been significantly boosted by FIFA's plan to increase financial contributions to member associations from $10 million to $25 million, a substantial figure for smaller Caribbean nations.</p>\n<p>Beyond direct financial support, FIFA won favor with the countries through investments in development initiatives like the FIFA Forward program. On Thursday, Infantino announced a $5.3 million investment in Aruba to build seven artificial turf pitches at clubs across the island.</p>\n<p>\"For CFU member associations, many of which continue to operate with limited financial and human resources, these programs have contributed to efforts to strengthen football development and create opportunities across the region,\" the statement added.</p>\n<p>An Associated Press tally published last month indicated that Infantino - even before the CFU's endorsement - was already closing in on a majority among FIFA's 211 member federations.</p>\n<p>Infantino's leadership of FIFA has come under intense scrutiny since July, when his secretive plan to sell stakes in the World Cup to private investors including Josh Kushner was revealed in media reports.</p>\n<p>A global backlash, including by senior FIFA executives, saw Infantino drop the project within days.</p>\n<p>\"The CFU offers its support with the expectation that FIFA will continue to strengthen accountability, uphold the highest standards of governance, and pursue the reforms necessary to ensure that every member association is fairly represented and served,\" the statement added.</p>\n\n\n\n\n","allowAMP":true,"allowAds":true,"allowComments":true,"allowCommerce":true,"allowContentReactions":true,"allowSearch":true,"byline":"Associated Press","isLiveBlog":false,"links":{"api":{"self":{"href":"https://content.core.api.espn.com/v1/sports/news/50402359"}},"app":{"sportscenter":{"href":"sportscenter://x-callback-url/showStory?uid=50402359"}},"mobile":{"href":"http://m.espn.go.com/soccer/story?storyId=50402359"},"web":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/soccer/story/_/id/50402359/infantino-secures-caribbean-support-fifa-reelection-bid"}},"premium":false},{"id":50398688,"nowId":"1-50398688","contentKey":"50398688-1-5-1","dataSourceIdentifier":"a89f1a4119059","publishedkey":"50398688","type":"HeadlineN